From: Christian Stewart <christian@aperture.us>
Subject: mythread: use sigprocmask on WASI with emulated signals

xz leaves mythread_sigmask undefined on WASI, which has no signal mask,
but signals.c calls it whenever threads are disabled. wasi-libc's
emulated signals provide sigprocmask, so use it there.

Signed-off-by: Christian Stewart <christian@aperture.us>
---
 src/common/mythread.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/mythread.h b/src/common/mythread.h
--- a/src/common/mythread.h
+++ b/src/common/mythread.h
@@ -79,7 +79,8 @@
 
 
 #if !(defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__CYGWIN__)) \
-		&& (!defined(__wasm__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__))
+		&& (!defined(__wasm__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) \
+			|| defined(_WASI_EMULATED_SIGNAL))
 // Use sigprocmask() to set the signal mask in single-threaded programs.
 #include <signal.h>
 
